// Caption module for Cross-Modality Deconvolution & Gene-Selection Supplementary Comparison Suite
// Note: All Consensus-Meta42 state labels omit M01–M42 numeric prefixes per manuscript convention.

#let caption_supp_deconv_factorial_matrix = [
  *Factorial deconvolution solver $times$ gene-selection benchmark across pure external bulk RNA-seq trials ($N = 965$ patients) and hierarchical cross-paradigm concordance across 13 single-cell references.*
  *(a)* Annotated $8 times 5$ factorial matrix evaluating five direct bulk RNA-seq deconvolution operators (`InstaPrism EM`, `DWLS` heteroscedastic dampened weighted least squares, `CIBERSORT` $nu$-SVR margin support genes, `Ridge Log-Contrast`, and the 4-solver `Ensemble`) across eight single-cell gene-selection and `GMRF` Laplacian resolvent $(bold(I) + bold(L)_("sym"))^(-1)$ architectures, stratified into four strict information-hygiene tiers: Tier I unsupervised native markers (`G0` cell-cycle/housekeeping filtered `HVG`, `G1` within-cohort unsupervised specificity; $r = +0.16$ to $+0.19$), Tier II strictly held-out cross-atlas Leave-One-Cohort-Out (`LOCO`) `milopy` transfer (`G2b` / `Alt 1`, zero target-cohort `milopy` input; $r = +0.20$ to $+0.26$, up to $8/9$ single-cell cohorts positive), Tier III state-blind cohort-shared `milopy` gene relevance (`G2a` / `Alt 2`, $w_g^((c)) >= 0$ shared identically across all states within cohort $c$; $r = +0.34$ to $+0.43$, $9/9$ cohorts positive), and Tier IV state-adaptive `milopy` specificity weighting (`G2d` / `Alt 3`–`Alt 4`, $W_(k,g) >= 0$; $r = +0.48$ to $+0.63$, $9/9$ cohorts positive), compared against the indirect whole-tumor `Gondal` bank transfer baseline (`D0`, $r = +0.20, rho = +0.21$, $6/9$ cohorts positive).
  *(b)* Reference granularity lift from fine-grained native Leiden clusters (`Unified-All9`, $N = 355$ states, circles) to the 42-state pan-cancer consensus dictionary (`Consensus-Meta42`, $K = 42$ states, diamonds) holding the `DWLS` solver constant across tiers, demonstrating consistent consensus variance reduction ($Delta r = +0.01$ to $+0.25$; `Alt 2` reaching $r = +0.65$ and `Alt 3`/`Alt 4` reaching $r = +0.72$–$0.74$ on pure external bulk RNA-seq).
  *(c)* Complete $10 times 13$ cross-paradigm $times$ single-cell reference Pearson $r$ concordance matrix comparing the three pseudobulk-calibrated cross-modality frameworks (`Option A: GMRF + DL` $r = +0.83$, `Option B Unsmoothed` $r = +0.68$, `Option B GMRF` $r = +0.67$) side-by-side against seven 100% pure external bulk RNA-seq frameworks across all nine individual single-cell cohorts (`Sade-Feldman`, `Gondal`, `Marteau`, `Yan`, `Hu`, `Liu`, `Hong`, `Luoma`, `Raufi`) and four pooled/consensus tiers (`Mel+PanCa`, `NSCLC-Uni`, `Unified-All9`, `Meta-42`). Cohort-native operators eliminate cross-compartment sign inversions in `CD45+`/`CD3+` FACS-sorted cohorts (`Sade-Feldman`: $-0.11 -> +0.29 -> +0.35 -> +0.65 -> +0.69$; `Luoma`: $-0.16 -> +0.63 -> +0.84$) and pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (`Raufi`: $-0.06 -> +0.22 -> +0.51$).
]

#let caption_supp_deconv_validation_suite = [
  *Four-axis methodological validation of pure external bulk RNA-seq deconvolution approaches: dual permutation null calibration, Leave-One-Trial-Out (`LOTO`) jackknife stability, single-cell pseudobulk compositional recovery, and out-of-trial clinical response prediction.*
  *(a) Validation V1 — Dual Permutation Null Calibration:* Empirical 95% null intervals (shaded bars, central square = null mean) under $B = 1,000$ within-trial bulk patient-response label permutations (`V1a`, centered at $0.000$ across all pure-bulk paradigms, confirming zero bulk outcome leakage into gene selection or reference construction; exact permutation $p = 0.040$ for `Alt 1` and $p = 0.004$–$0.007$ for `Alt 2`–`Alt 4`) paired with active target-cohort single-cell state-label re-weighting permutation means (`V1b`, diamonds), which remain identically centered at $0.000$ for unsupervised (`D0`, `G0`, `G1`) and cross-atlas `LOCO` (`Alt 1`, `Alt 1b`) operators, rise moderately to $+0.20$ for state-blind cohort-shared (`Alt 2`, confirming $> +0.21$ excess bulk alignment above shared gene filtering), and transparently quantify the state-prior alignment baseline ($+0.52$–$0.59$) of state-adaptive operators (`Alt 3`, `Alt 4`).
  *(b) Validation V3 — 11-Trial `LOTO` Bulk Jackknife Stability:* Global cross-modality Pearson $r$ recomputed after holding out each individual external clinical trial in turn (`Hugo`, `Riaz`, `Liu`, `Gide`, `Rosenberg`, `Padron`, `Anders`, `McDermott`, `Choueiri`, `Jung`, and `Cho`; points = 11 held-out folds, horizontal bars = min–max range, diamonds = full 11-trial estimate), confirming narrow jackknife intervals (e.g., `Alt 2`: $[+0.40, +0.42]$; `Alt 3`: $[+0.59, +0.62]$; `Alt 4`: $[+0.62, +0.65]$) and absence of single-trial leverage fragility.
  *(c) Validation V2 — Single-Cell Pseudobulk Ground-Truth Compositional Recovery vs. External Bulk Concordance:* Two-objective landscape across all 41 pure-bulk candidates comparing per-patient centered log-ratio (`CLR`) fraction recovery on $N = 613$ ground-truth single-cell pseudobulk biopsies against external bulk `milopy` concordance ($N = 355$ states), showing that cohort-native operators substantially improve ground-truth compositional fidelity ($r_("PB") = 0.38$–$0.50$) relative to indirect `Gondal` bank transfer (`D0`, $r_("PB") = 0.35$) while illustrating the variance trade-off between neutral-state reconstruction (`G0`/`G1`) and responder-axis signal concentration (`G2b`/`G2a`/`G2d`).
  *(d) Validation V4 — Out-of-Fold (`LOTO`) External Bulk Clinical Response Prediction:* Sample-size-weighted mean `ROC-AUC` (bars) and individual held-out trial test `ROC-AUC` values (circles scaled by trial sample size $N_t$, dashed vertical line = $0.50$ random baseline) when training linear responder weights strictly on 10 external bulk trials and predicting clinical response in the 11th held-out trial ($N = 965$ patients; mean `LOTO ROC-AUC` $= 0.598$–$0.613$ across pure-bulk operators).
]

#let caption_supp_deconv_head_to_head = [
  *Head-to-head comparison across eight flagship cross-modality deconvolution paradigms: global 355-state concordance scatters, $9 times 9$ inter-method rank agreement, and canonical `Consensus-Meta42` biomarker polarity stability.*
  *(a)* Identically scaled ($[-3.8, +3.8]$) small-multiples scatter grid comparing within-cohort $z$-normalized single-cell `milopy` differential abundance against within-cohort $z$-normalized `Pan-iAtlas-Meta` bulk deconvolution responder $hat(beta)$ across all $N = 355$ fine-grained cell states (coloured by the nine single-cell cohorts with OLS trendlines) for `(a1)` `Option A: GMRF + DL` ($r = +0.83, rho = +0.85, 9/9+$), `(a2)` `Option B: Unsmoothed` ($r = +0.68, rho = +0.65, 9/9+$), `(a3)` `Option C: D0 Baseline` ($r = +0.20, rho = +0.21, 6/9+$), `(a4)` `Unsup. G1 + InstaPrism` ($r = +0.19, rho = +0.19, 7/9+$), `(a5)` `Alt 1: LOCO + NuSVR` ($r = +0.24, rho = +0.26, 8/9+$), `(a6)` `Alt 2: Cohort + DWLS` ($r = +0.42, rho = +0.45, 9/9+$), `(a7)` `Alt 3: State + GMRF` ($r = +0.61, rho = +0.68, 9/9+$), and `(a8)` `Alt 4: State + DWLS` ($r = +0.63, rho = +0.70, 9/9+$).
  *(b)* Symmetric $9 times 9$ pairwise Spearman rank-correlation matrix ($rho$) across the 42 `Consensus-Meta42` inferred state effect vectors, anchored against single-cell `milopy` (`SC Milopy`) in the first row and column, demonstrating strong rank convergence between `SC Milopy` and `Alt 2`, `Alt 3`, `Alt 4`, and `Option A` ($rho = 0.69$–$0.86$, inter-operator `Alt 2`–`Alt 4` $rho = 0.89$–$0.99$).
  *(c)* Standardized effect-size ($z$) and directional polarity stability matrix across `SC Milopy` and all eight deconvolution paradigms for the 14 canonical `Consensus-Meta42` responder-enriched (`CR2+PAX5+ TLS B`, `MS4A1+CD79A+ TLS B`, `JCHAIN+MZB1+ Plasma`, `CXCL13+NMB+ Tfh/Trm`, `CXCL13+PDCD1+ Tex`, `GZMK+NKG7+ Tem CD8+`, `CXCL9+STAT1+ M1-TAM`) and non-responder-enriched (`MRC1+CD163+ M2-TAM`, `VEGFA+KDR+ Endo.`, `S100A8+CXCL8+ MDSC`, `CA9+SLC2A1+ Hypox.`, `VIM+ZEB1+ EMT Tumor`, `ISLR+COL5A2+ myCAF`, `FAP+TGFB1+ Mat. CAF`) states, confirming invariant biological conclusions across model formulations.
]

#let caption_supp_deconv_gene_mechanisms = [
  *Mechanistic basis of cross-modality gene-space concordance, `CD45+` FACS-sorted melanoma cohort rescue, and cumulative pure-bulk architectural ablation.*
  *(a)* Cross-platform gene-space concordance across $U = 4,529$ union reference genes plotting pan-single-cell `milopy` state specificity alignment ($overline(r)_g^("SC")$) against the 11-trial external bulk RNA-seq random-effects responder meta-$z$ statistic ($z_g^("bulk")$), separating conserved immune/TLS responder drivers (_CXCL13_, _CXCL9_, _MS4A1_, _CR2_, _JCHAIN_) and conserved fibrotic/myCAF non-responder drivers (_FAP_, _COL5A2_) from discordant cell-cycle, immediate-early dissociation, ribosomal, and exocrine confounders (_MKI67_, _TOP2A_, _UBE2C_, _FOS_) where bulk proliferation reflects malignant tumor cycling rather than clonal T-cell expansion.
  *(b)* State-level mechanistic rescue in `CD45+` FACS-sorted melanoma (`Sade-Feldman` `GSE120575`, $K = 38$ immune states): indirect whole-tumor bank projection (`D0 GondalBank`, $r = -0.11$) assigns muted or inverted bulk responder shifts to `CR2+PAX5+ TLS B` and lymphoid subsets due to cross-compartment collinearity in the 355-state tumor+stroma bank, whereas cohort-native immune operators (`Alt 1: LOCO + NuSVR`, $r = +0.29$; `Alt 2: Cohort Milo + DWLS`, $r = +0.35$) restore positive cross-modality concordance (vertical dashed rescue trajectories).
  *(c)* Stepwise cumulative ablation across all nine architectural milestones from unsupervised native pure-bulk deconvolution (`Step 1`, $r = +0.19$, `Meta-42` $r = +0.23$) and baseline `Option C` (`Step 2`, $r = +0.20$, `Meta-42` $r = +0.34$) through cross-atlas `LOCO` (`Steps 3–4`, $r = +0.24$–$0.26$), state-blind cohort-shared `DWLS` (`Step 5`, $r = +0.42$, `Meta-42` $r = +0.65$), and state-adaptive `DWLS` (`Steps 6–7`, $r = +0.61$–$0.63$, `Meta-42` $r = +0.72$–$0.74$), contextualized against pseudobulk-calibrated `Option B` (`Step 8`, $r = +0.68$) and `Option A` (`Step 9`, $r = +0.83$, `Meta-42` $r = +0.90$).
]

